      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Thinking the debutants hold the key in this race. JUNIPER (8) is a half to two winners on debut for the Williams stable, with Pike sticking from both trials coming into this. She's shown enough there to suggest she has some ability and this set-up looks nice for her. Can make an immediate impact. STAR SEED (10) is another debutant, this time out of the Fiore stable. She won her latest trial at Lark Hill in impressive fashion and looks to be improving every time she steps out. Maps to get every chance and a forward showing is on the cards. AMALIE'S RULE (7) has the race experience and turned in a better effort last start despite jumping a 30-1 chance. That rating is solid and she finally draws a handy gate. Wouldn't surprise to see her improve. KEPPEL GATE (9) won her latest trial with Pike on board, but Pike elects to ride JUNIPER. Recent trial was impressive though and she can't be discounted.",
